            },
            "view": "welcome"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s2-p1",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "Telemachus, Penelope and Odysseus’s son, welcomed a stranger into the hall and offered him bread."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s2-p2",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "The house still belonged to his father. He wanted it to remember how to welcome a guest."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s2-p3",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "The stranger was really Athena, a goddess helping Odysseus’s family. She had changed her appearance to visit the house."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s2-p4",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "dialogue",
          "who": "telemachus",
          "text": "“Eat first. You can tell me where you have come from afterward.”",
          "listener": "athena"
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s2-p5",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "dialogue",
          "who": "athena",
          "text": "“And where would you go, if you could leave?”",
          "listener": "telemachus"
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s2-p6",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "dialogue",
          "who": "telemachus",
          "text": "“Somewhere a person might have seen my father.”",
          "listener": "athena"
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s2-p7",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "dialogue",
          "who": "athena",
          "text": "“Then ask. A son can seek an answer, even when a house has learned to wait.”",
          "listener": "telemachus"
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s2-look-toward-the-door",
          "type": "action",
          "duration": 800,
          "effects": {
            "actors": {
              "telemachus": {
                "facing": "back"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s2-p8",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "Telemachus turned toward the doorway."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s2-p9",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "For years, he had watched it for someone coming in. Now he imagined himself going out."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s2-leave-the-moment",
