        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s5-p1",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "Meanwhile, back in Ithaca, Eurycleia told Penelope that Telemachus had sailed. He was still away on his search."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s5-p2",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "dialogue",
          "who": "penelope",
          "text": "“You knew?”",
          "listener": "eurycleia"
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s5-p3",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "dialogue",
          "who": "eurycleia",
          "text": "“He asked me to wait before telling you. He feared that you would grieve.”",
          "listener": "penelope"
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s5-p4",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "dialogue",
          "who": "penelope",
          "text": "“And so he left me to do it afterward.”",
          "listener": "eurycleia"
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s5-p5",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "narration",
          "who": null,
          "text": "Eurycleia stayed beside her. There was no answer that could make a mother less afraid."
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s5-p6",
          "type": "text",
          "kind": "dialogue",
          "who": "eurycleia",
          "text": "“He took provisions. He found companions. He prepared, my lady.”",
          "listener": "penelope"
        },
        {
          "id": "odyssey-c2-s5-return-to-the-stool",
          "type": "action",
          "duration": 1000,
          "effects": {
